; State flags of the bell, three levers and the wheel of faith ($851B-$8520)
;
; One byte for each of the interactive items (type 4, 9 and 10 of the item types, see #R$8EDF). They are read by the
; item routines, which choose the sprite frame from them, and by the room scripts (ops $95 and $9C test a byte through
; its address, #R$A04B and #R$A058), which open or close doors and remove blocks.
; .
; +0 BellRung ($851B): 0, or 1 once the bell of the Tower of the Bell (room 2) has been touched (#R$A748, sound 3).
; The script of room 8 (The Altar) erases a 2x2 block of wall at row 20, column 26 when it is set.
; +1 LeverRoom9 ($851C): 0 or 1, the lever of room 9 (Hangman tree). While it is 0 the script of room 20 draws a door
; at the left edge (#R$7F87).
; +2 LeverRoom10 ($851D): 0 or 1, the lever of room 10 (Pestilent Beast). While it is 0 the script of room 8 draws a
; door at its right edge (#R$778A).
; +3 WheelState ($851E): the wheel of faith in room 17: 0 at rest, $06 once turned; each touch toggles bits 1-2 (XOR
; $86) and bit 7 is set while the player still touches it (#R$A6A1). It decides which crosses can be picked up: the
; crosses of type 1 only while it is 0, those of type 2 only while it is not (#R$A782, #R$A777), and which of the two
; cross shapes is drawn.
; +4 LeverRoom20 ($851F): 0 or 1, the lever of room 20 (Unexpected gate). While it is 0 the script of room 20 draws a
; door at its right edge (#R$778A).
; +5 $8520: unused
@label=BellRung
g$851B DEFB $00
@label=LeverRoom9
 $851C DEFB $00
@label=LeverRoom10
 $851D DEFB $00
@label=WheelState
 $851E DEFB $00
@label=LeverRoom20
 $851F DEFB $00
 $8520 DEFB $00
